IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, sections 3, 4 and 4.1 -- WHERE THE ACT APPLIES.
--
-- Section 3 says what a "province providing a comprehensive pension plan" and a "provincial pension
-- plan" are, and when a province becomes one. Section 4 says that the Act's contribution provisions
-- do not reach employment in such a province, or self-employed persons resident in one, with the
-- exceptions of subsection (2), the agreements of subsection (3), the rule of subsection (4) for where
-- an employee is employed and the rule of subsection (5) for the last day of the year. Section 4.1 lets
-- the Minister of National Revenue use electronic means.
--
-- The seat is the individual. The questions here are the ones a worker or self-employed person asks
-- first: does the Act's contribution regime reach my employment, or me for this year, at all? The
-- province's own status ("a province providing a comprehensive pension plan") comes from a regulation
-- that is not among the texts this encoding reads, so a caller normally supplies it directly as the
-- flag on the Province record. Rule `s 3(1) — a province providing a comprehensive pension plan`
-- works the flag out from the facts the definition lists, for a caller that has them (NOTES.md,
-- fork register, F3).
--
-- The Act never names a province, and neither does this module.

§ `Sections 3 to 4.1 -- where the Act applies`

§§ `Section 3(1) -- province providing a comprehensive pension plan, provincial pension plan`

-- src:93 | (a) the government of which has, on or before May 3, 1965, signified the intention of that province to provide for the establishment and operation in that province, in lieu of the operation therein of this Act, of a plan of old age pensions and supplementary benefits providing for the making of contributions thereunder commencing with the year 1966 and providing for the payment of benefits thereunder comparable to those provided by this Act, or
-- src:94 | (b) the government of which has, at any time after May 3, 1965, given notice in writing to the Minister of Employment and Social Development of the intention of that province to provide
@ref Act s 3(1) "province providing a comprehensive pension plan", paragraphs (a) and (b) (src:93-94)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 3(1) — the date that divides paragraph (a) from paragraph (b)` MEANS YearMonthDay 1965 5 3

-- src:91 | 3 (1) In this Act,
-- src:92 | province providing a comprehensive pension plan means a province prescribed by a regulation made on the recommendation of the Minister of Employment and Social Development for the purposes of this Act as a province
-- src:93 | (a) the government of which has, on or before May 3, 1965, signified the intention of that province to provide for the establishment and operation in that province, in lieu of the operation therein of this Act, of a plan of old age pensions and supplementary benefits providing for the making of contributions thereunder commencing with the year 1966 and providing for the payment of benefits thereunder comparable to those provided by this Act, or
-- src:94 | (b) the government of which has, at any time after May 3, 1965, given notice in writing to the Minister of Employment and Social Development of the intention of that province to provide
-- src:95 | (i) for the establishment and operation in that province, in lieu of the operation therein of this Act, of a plan of old age pensions and supplementary benefits providing for the making of contributions thereunder commencing with the third year following the year in which the notice was given and providing for the payment of benefits thereunder comparable to those then provided by this Act or by any provincial pension plan other than that plan, and
-- src:96 | (ii) for the assumption under that plan of all obligations and liabilities accrued or accruing to the first day of that third year with respect to the payment of benefits under this Act attributable to contributions made under this Act in respect of employment in that province or in respect of self-employed earnings of persons resident in that province; (province instituant un régime général de pensions)
@ref Act s 3(1) "province providing a comprehensive pension plan" (src:91-96)
GIVEN `prescribed by a regulation made on the recommendation of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date the government signified its intention` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date the government gave written notice` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `year in which contributions under the plan begin` IS A NUMBER
      `the benefits are comparable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan assumes the obligations and liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(1) — a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `prescribed by a regulation made on the recommendation of the Minister` `date the government signified its intention` `date the government gave written notice` `year in which contributions under the plan begin` `the benefits are comparable` `the plan assumes the obligations and liabilities` MEANS
    `prescribed by a regulation made on the recommendation of the Minister` AND (`paragraph (a) is met` OR `paragraph (b) is met`)
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a) is met` MEANS
            CONSIDER `date the government signified its intention`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST signified THEN (signified AT MOST `s 3(1) — the date that divides paragraph (a) from paragraph (b)`) AND (`year in which contributions under the plan begin` EQUALS 1966) AND `the benefits are comparable`
        `paragraph (b) is met` MEANS
            CONSIDER `date the government gave written notice`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST notice THEN (NOT (notice AT MOST `s 3(1) — the date that divides paragraph (a) from paragraph (b)`)) AND (`year in which contributions under the plan begin` EQUALS ((DATE_YEAR notice) PLUS 3)) AND `the benefits are comparable` AND `the plan assumes the obligations and liabilities`

-- src:97 | provincial pension plan means a plan of old age pensions and supplementary benefits for the establishment and operation of which provision has been made as described in paragraph (a) or (b) of the definition province providing a comprehensive pension plan under a law of a province providing a comprehensive pension plan. (régime provincial de pensions)
@ref Act s 3(1) "provincial pension plan" (src:97)
GIVEN `provision has been made as described in paragraph (a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under a law of a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(1) — a provincial pension plan` `provision has been made as described in paragraph (a) or (b)` `under a law of a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` MEANS
    `provision has been made as described in paragraph (a) or (b)` AND `under a law of a province providing a comprehensive pension plan`

§§ `Sections 3(2) and 3(3) -- prescription of a province after notice, and when it takes effect`

-- src:99 | (2) Notwithstanding anything in subsection (1), where, not later than twelve months before the first day of the third year following the year in which notice in writing as described in paragraph (b) of the definition province providing a comprehensive pension plan in subsection (1) was given to the Minister of Employment and Social Development by the government of a province, the legislature of the province has provided by law for the establishment and operation in that province of a plan of old age pensions and supplementary benefits as described in that paragraph and for the assumption under that plan of all obligations and liabilities accrued or accruing as described in that paragraph, the Governor in Council shall, by regulation made on the recommendation of the Minister of Employment and Social Development for the purposes of this Act, prescribe that province as a province described in that paragraph.
@ref Act s 3(2) (src:99)
GIVEN `date the government gave written notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 3(2) — the last day by which the legislature must have provided by law` `date the government gave written notice` MEANS
    `the date a time limit before a date goes back to` (YearMonthDay ((DATE_YEAR `date the government gave written notice`) PLUS 3) 1 1) (`a number of months` WITH `number of months` IS 12)

@ref Act s 3(2) (src:99)
GIVEN `date the government gave written notice` IS A DATE
      `date the legislature provided by law` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the law provides for the plan and for the assumption of obligations and liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(2) — the Governor in Council must prescribe the province` `date the government gave written notice` `date the legislature provided by law` `the law provides for the plan and for the assumption of obligations and liabilities` MEANS
    `the law provides for the plan and for the assumption of obligations and liabilities` AND `the law was made in time`
    WHERE
        `the law was made in time` MEANS
            CONSIDER `date the legislature provided by law`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST enacted THEN enacted AT MOST (`s 3(2) — the last day by which the legislature must have provided by law` `date the government gave written notice`)

-- src:101 | (3) Any regulation made pursuant to subsection (2) becomes effective on the first day of the third year following the year in which the notice referred to in that subsection was given to the Minister of Employment and Social Development.
@ref Act s 3(3) (src:101)
GIVEN `date the government gave written notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 3(3) — the day a regulation under subsection (2) becomes effective` `date the government gave written notice` MEANS
    YearMonthDay ((DATE_YEAR `date the government gave written notice`) PLUS 3) 1 1

§§ `Section 4(1) -- the Act's contribution provisions and a province providing a comprehensive pension plan`

-- src:103 | 4 (1) Notwithstanding anything in this Act, except as provided in subsection (2),
-- src:104 | (a) the provisions of this Act with respect to the making of contributions by employees and employers in respect of pensionable employment and the provisions of Part III with respect to employees in pensionable employment do not apply in relation to employment in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan; and
@ref Act s 4(1)(a) (src:103-104)
GIVEN `the employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (2) treats the employment as employment in another province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4(1)(a) — the Act's provisions on employee and employer contributions reach the employment` `the employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `subsection (2) treats the employment as employment in another province` MEANS
    (NOT `the employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan`) OR `subsection (2) treats the employment as employment in another province`

-- src:105 | (b) the provisions of this Act with respect to the making of contributions by persons for any year in respect of self-employed earnings do not apply in relation to persons who on the last day of that year were resident in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan.
@ref Act s 4(1)(b) (src:105)
GIVEN `the province in which the person was resident on the last day of the year` IS A MAYBE Province
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4(1)(b) — the Act's provisions on self-employed contributions reach the person for the year` `the province in which the person was resident on the last day of the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the province in which the person was resident on the last day of the year`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST province THEN NOT (province's `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan`)

§§ `Sections 4(2) and 4(3) -- employment the Act still reaches, and the agreements`

-- src:107 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), all of the provisions of this Act apply to
-- src:108 | (a) employment by Her Majesty in right of Canada or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of Canada in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan, and
-- src:109 | (b) any employment in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan if and to the extent that the establishment and operation of the plan referred to in paragraph (a) or (b) of the definition province providing a comprehensive pension plan in subsection 3(1), as the case may be, in relation to persons employed in that employment is outside the legislative authority of the legislature of that province,
-- src:110 | as though that employment were employment in a province other than a province providing a comprehensive pension plan.
@ref Act s 4(2) (src:107-110)
GIVEN `the employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `employment by Her Majesty in right of Canada or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provincial plan in relation to persons employed in the employment is outside the legislative authority of the province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4(2) — the employment is described in subsection (2)` `the employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `employment by Her Majesty in right of Canada or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of Canada` `the provincial plan in relation to persons employed in the employment is outside the legislative authority of the province` MEANS
    `the employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` AND (`employment by Her Majesty in right of Canada or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of Canada` OR `the provincial plan in relation to persons employed in the employment is outside the legislative authority of the province`)

-- src:112 | (3) The Minister of Employment and Social Development, with the approval of the Governor in Council, may on behalf of the Government of Canada enter into an agreement with the government of a province providing a comprehensive pension plan whereby, in accordance with such terms and conditions as may be set out in the agreement, any persons employed in employment described in subsection (2), and any employers of any persons employed in such employment, with respect to any persons so employed, shall be subject to the provisions of the provincial pension plan of that province in all respects as though the establishment and operation of that plan in relation to any persons so employed were within the legislative authority of the legislature of that province, and with respect to any period while the agreement continues in force, the agreement has the force of law according to the provisions thereof.
@ref Act s 4(3) (src:112)
GIVEN `the employment is described in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an agreement under subsection (3) is in force for the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4(3) — the employment is subject to the provincial pension plan under an agreement` `the employment is described in subsection (2)` `an agreement under subsection (3) is in force for the employment` MEANS
    `the employment is described in subsection (2)` AND `an agreement under subsection (3) is in force for the employment`

@ref Act s 4(2) "Subject to subsection (3)" (src:107)
GIVEN `the employment is described in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an agreement under subsection (3) is in force for the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4(2) — the Act applies to the employment as though it were employment in another province` `the employment is described in subsection (2)` `an agreement under subsection (3) is in force for the employment` MEANS
    `the employment is described in subsection (2)` AND (NOT `an agreement under subsection (3) is in force for the employment`)

§§ `Sections 4(4) and 4(5) -- where a person is employed, and the last day of the year`

-- src:114 | (4) For the purposes of this Act, a person shall be deemed to be employed in the province in which the establishment of his employer to which he reports for work is situated, and where the employee is not required to report for work at any establishment of his employer, he shall be deemed to be employed in the province in which the establishment of his employer from which his remuneration is paid is situated.
@ref Act s 4(4) (src:114)
GIVEN `the province of the establishment to which the employee reports for work` IS A MAYBE Province
      `the province of the establishment from which the remuneration is paid` IS A Province
GIVETH A Province
`s 4(4) — the province in which a person is deemed employed` `the province of the establishment to which the employee reports for work` `the province of the establishment from which the remuneration is paid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the province of the establishment to which the employee reports for work`
    WHEN JUST reporting THEN reporting
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the province of the establishment from which the remuneration is paid`

-- src:116 | (5) A reference in paragraph (1)(b) to the last day of a year shall, in the case of a person who resided in Canada at any time in that year but ceased to reside in Canada before the last day thereof, be deemed to be a reference to the last day in that year on which he resided in Canada.
@ref Act s 4(5) (src:116)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `last day in the year on which the person resided in Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 4(5) — the day taken as the last day of a year for paragraph (1)(b)` year `last day in the year on which the person resided in Canada` MEANS
    CONSIDER `last day in the year on which the person resided in Canada`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the last day of the year`
    WHEN JUST resided THEN
        IF resided AT LEAST `the last day of the year`
        THEN `the last day of the year`
        ELSE resided
    WHERE
        `the last day of the year` MEANS YearMonthDay year 12 31

§§ `Section 4.1 -- electronic means`

-- src:120 | 4.1 The Minister of National Revenue may use electronic means to create, communicate, make available, collect, receive, store or otherwise deal with documents or information under this Act.
@ref Act s 4.1 (src:120)
GIVEN minister IS A Minister
      `the document or information is dealt with under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4.1 — this section permits the Minister to use electronic means` minister `the document or information is dealt with under this Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER minister
    WHEN `the Minister of National Revenue` THEN `the document or information is dealt with under this Act`
    WHEN `the Minister of Employment and Social Development` THEN FALSE
